@monthly_briefing
title: Political Strategy
subtitle: Italy — [+ month : month +] / [+ year +]
new-page: true
is-hand: true
max-cards: 3

POLITICAL STRATEGY

Your party: [+ party_name +]

Your party must respond to economic pressure, political violence and declining confidence in public institutions. Whether you govern, support a coalition or lead the opposition, draw strategy cards and choose which initiatives to pursue.

[? if year = 1969 and month = 12 : **Historical briefing — Piazza Fontana.** On 12 December, a bomb explodes at the Banca Nazionale dell'Agricoltura in Milan, killing 17 people and injuring many more. The attack intensifies fear, suspicion and political polarisation. ?]
[? if year = 1970 and month = 5 : **Historical briefing — Workers' Statute.** Parliament approves major protections for workers' rights, reflecting years of labour mobilisation. ?]
[? if year = 1970 and month = 7 : **Historical briefing — Reggio Calabria unrest.** Protests erupt over the designation of Catanzaro as the regional capital, developing into months of street clashes and unrest. ?]
[? if year = 1972 and month = 5 : **Historical briefing — General election.** The Christian Democrats remain the largest party as Italy's party system faces pressure from polarisation and political violence. ?]
[? if year = 1973 and month = 10 : **Historical briefing — Oil crisis.** The international oil shock places new pressure on prices, production and household budgets. ?]
[? if year = 1974 and month = 5 : **Historical briefing — Divorce referendum.** Voters reject the proposal to repeal Italy's divorce law, delivering a major defeat to conservative campaigners. ?]
[? if year = 1974 and month = 8 : **Historical briefing — Italicus bombing.** A bomb on the Italicus express train kills 12 people, deepening public fear of political terrorism. ?]
[? if year = 1976 and month = 6 : **Historical briefing — General election.** The Christian Democrats remain ahead while the Communist Party achieves a major electoral result, sharpening debate over whether it can be brought closer to government. ?]
[? if year = 1978 and month = 3 : **Historical briefing — Aldo Moro kidnapped.** Red Brigades kidnap the former prime minister on 16 March and kill five members of his escort. The crisis places extraordinary pressure on the state. ?]
[? if year = 1978 and month = 5 : **Historical briefing — Moro murdered.** After 55 days in captivity, Aldo Moro is found dead on 9 May. The killing leaves a lasting wound in Italian political life. ?]
[? if year = 1980 and month = 8 : **Historical briefing — Bologna station bombing.** On 2 August, a bomb kills 85 people at Bologna Centrale railway station. The country demands answers and accountability. ?]
[? if year = 1981 and month = 5 : **Historical briefing — P2 scandal.** The discovery of the P2 masonic lodge's membership lists exposes a clandestine network with links to powerful figures and triggers a political crisis. ?]
[? if year = 1982 and month = 9 : **Historical briefing — Dalla Chiesa assassinated.** General Carlo Alberto dalla Chiesa, his wife and a police escort are killed in Palermo on 3 September, underscoring the threat posed by organised crime. ?]
[? if year = 1983 and month = 6 : **Historical briefing — General election.** The June election weakens the Christian Democrats and opens the way to a new political arrangement, with Bettino Craxi becoming prime minister in August. ?]

